; TERM.term.un — the PATHS-LOCAL subset of verisectorium/template/TERM.term.un
; (proposed home: beside the entries it shapes; steward may relocate)
;
; This corpus uses the universal template minus what has no consumer here yet:
; no :register (single-register corpus), no ui/api designation channels, no
; :value-type/:constraints (no scored quantities among current terms), no
; |context-sentence (deferred until the checker can harvest them). Everything
; kept means something to bin/refresh-lexicon or to the D5 projection design.
;
; PATHS-LOCAL CONVENTIONS on top of the universal template:
;  - :subject-field is always addressing (kept anyway: the homograph fence
;    matters at the estate level — see perspective's |collision).
;  - |definition :defined-by must agree with the .md entry / segment "Terms
;    defined here" declarations; bin/refresh-lexicon checks this.
;  - |set-rel edges are the Euler-diagram substrate: a renderer may emit
;    diagrams from subset-of/disjoint-from/overlaps/partitions edges alone.
;  - |rel accepts a :one-of [a b c] qualifier when a relation's MANNER is a
;    closed enum (path's origin: explicit | implicit | universal) — one seat
;    with a qualified manner, never three relation kinds (which would triple
;    the seat and make {1,1} arity inexpressible).
;  - |formal :notation uses <latex:...> envelopes (dialect renders; carried
;    inert until then, per the frozen-bare-set discipline).
;
; See the universal template for field semantics, arities, and the WHY notes.
